    "answer": "## Findings\n\n### What \"surface-setup-check\" refers to\n\nThe codebase has no literal `surface-setup-check` type or class. The concept maps to the **mechanical pre-verify gate** executed at the start of stage 10 (Verify) before the agent runs. This gate comprises three sequential checks in `RunStage10PreAgentAsync` (`RelayDriver.Stage9.cs`):\n\n1. **Bootstrap check** (`RelayDriver.Bootstrap.cs`) \u2014 A smoke command (e.g. `nix develop --command true`) that validates the project's environment/toolchain is intact. Auto-detected from manifest globs (`flake.nix`, `*.nix`, `Brewfile`, `Dockerfile*`, `.tool-versions`, `rust-toolchain*`), or configured explicitly via `BootstrapCheckCommand` / `BootstrapFiles` in `.relay/config.json`.\n\n2. **New-guard probe** (`RelayDriver.RepoGuards.cs`, `NewGuardProbeAsync`) \u2014 Executes any guard scripts matching `NewGuardPatterns` in the manifest (default `tools/guards/**/*.sh`). These are project-specific gate scripts the author opts into.\n\n3. **Guard check** (`RelayDriver.RepoGuards.cs`, `IntegrateGuardAsync`) \u2014 Runs the configured `GuardCommand` (e.g. file-size guard, format verification). Supports baseline diffing so pre-existing violations don't block new work.\n\nAny of these can fail, and their outputs are combined into structured failure artifacts.\n\n### Existing failure/diagnostics architecture (well-developed)\n\n- **`RelayDriver.FailureOutput.cs`** \u2014 Centralizes failure text assembly: `BuildFailureOutput` (distilled tail for the agent prompt), `BuildFullFailureOutput` (complete log for the persisted artifact), and `BuildCombinedFailure` (shared section order: test failure \u2192 guard output \u2192 new guard probe \u2192 bootstrap output).\n\n- **`RelayDriver.VerifyObservability.cs`** \u2014 `PublishVerifyResultAsync` persists full output to `stageN-attemptM.verify-output.txt` files and emits a `verify_result` structured event carrying `command`, `exitCode`, `check` (red/green), `reason`, `treeHash`, and `outputFile` path. `TryPersistVerifyOutput` writes the artifact with a header (check verdict, capture timestamp, byte count).\n\n- **`ProcessRunners.Diagnostics.cs`** (`SwivalSubagentRunner.ExtractFailureReason`) \u2014 Sophisticated output distiller that filters nono's per-run advisory noise, strong/weak failure markers, proxy-log fallback for model-backend errors, and launch-failure detection.\n\n- **`ErrorHintClassifier.cs`** \u2014 Maps known failure signatures to actionable hints (connection refused \u2192 \"is the LiteLLM proxy running?\", timeout \u2192 \"raise maxTurns\", missing binary \u2192 \"install swival/nono\"). Used by `FlagAsync`.\n\n- **`RelayDriver.FlaggedWork.cs`** / `FlaggedWorkStore` \u2014 On flag, captures the full working tree state into a bundle so resume can restore context.\n\n- **`RelayDriver.Events.cs`** \u2014 `FlagAsync` writes a `NEEDS-REVIEW` marker, updates status entries, publishes a `flagged` event with reason, and returns a `Flagged` outcome. The `Stage10PreAgentData` record (in `RelayDriver.Stage9.cs`) bundles all pre-agent check results into a single typed object.\n\n- **Fix-verify loop** (`RelayDriver.VerifyFix.cs`) \u2014 On red Verify (stage 10), enters stage 11 escalation loop that re-runs with bumped tier/turns, re-checking bootstrap and guard on each iteration. Each iteration produces its own `verify-output.txt` artifact.\n\n- **Structured events** (`RelayEvent`) carry `Data` dictionaries with typed fields, consumed by the GUI.\n\n### Key code locations\n\n| Concern | File(s) |\n|---|---|\n| Bootstrap check logic | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.Bootstrap.cs` |\n| Guard check + new-guard probe | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.RepoGuards.cs` |\n| Pre-agent gate orchestration | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.Stage9.cs` |\n| Failure output assembly | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.FailureOutput.cs` |\n| Verify result publishing | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.VerifyObservability.cs` |\n| Fix-verify escalation loop | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.VerifyFix.cs` |\n| Flag/NEEDS-REVIEW logic | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.Events.cs` |\n| Flagged work capture | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayDriver.FlaggedWork.cs` |\n| Output distillation | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/ProcessRunners.Diagnostics.cs` |\n| Error hint classification | `src/VisualRelay.Domain/ErrorHintClassifier.cs` |\n| Stage definitions | `src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/RelayStages.cs` |\n| Config (maxStageFailures, bootstrap, guard) | `src/VisualRelay.Domain/RelayConfig.cs` |\n| Test run result model | `src/VisualRelay.Domain/TestRunResult.cs` |\n| Subagent result model | `src/VisualRelay.Domain/SubagentResult.cs` |\n| Artifact contracts | `docs/relay-artifacts.md` |\n\n### Constraints\n\n1. **File size guard**: Every C# source file must stay under 300 lines (`tools/VisualRelay.Guards`). New code must be split into focused partial files.\n2. **nono sandbox**: The sandbox restricts filesystem access; all code runs inside kernel-enforced boundaries (Landlock/Seatbelt).\n3. **Event-driven observability**: The only way to surface failure info to the GUI is through `RelayEvent` with structured `Data` dictionaries. Must also write files if persistence across runs is needed.\n4. **Artifact contract** (`docs/relay-artifacts.md`): The file layout and naming under `.relay/<taskId>/` is load-bearing. Verify output files follow `stageN-attemptM.verify-output.txt` convention.\n5. **`NEEDS-REVIEW` marker**: The sole persistent \"this task failed\" signal for queue drain avoidance. Any new failure surface must not break this protocol.\n6. **Stage pipeline is fixed**: The 12 stages in `RelayStages.cs` (1\u201312) are immutable \u2014 a new \"setup-check\" stage cannot be inserted without changing the whole pipeline design.\n7. **Bootstrap/guard are opt-in via config**: Projects may not configure them at all (null \u2192 skip). The system must handle absent checks gracefully.\n8. **Partial class pattern**: `RelayDriver` is split across ~15 partial files. New functionality must follow this pattern.\n9. **C# / .NET 10 / Avalonia**: The tech stack limits frontend changes to Avalonia XAML + C# view models; backend changes go in `VisualRelay.Core`.\n10. **`MaxStageFailures` cap**: The fix-verify loop runs at most `MaxStageFailures` iterations (default 3) before flagging. Any new failure details must fit within this bounded retry budget.\n11. **BaselineVerify mode**: Pre-existing guard/test failures can be excluded via baseline diffing; failure details must distinguish new vs. pre-existing failures.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"findings\": \"The codebase has no literal 'surface-setup-check' concept. It maps to the mechanical pre-verify gate at stage 10 (Verify) comprising: bootstrap check (environment toolchain smoke test), new-guard probe (project-specific gate scripts), and guard check (policy rules like file-size limits). Each check can fail independently; their outputs are combined via BuildCombinedFailure in RelayDriver.FailureOutput.cs into a structured format. The existing diagnostics architecture is already sophisticated: output distillation (ProcessRunners.Diagnostics.cs) filters nono noise and extracts failure markers; ErrorHintClassifier.cs maps failure signatures to actionable hints; PublishVerifyResultAsync persists full output to stageN-attemptM.verify-output.txt artifacts and emits structured verify_result events; the fix-verify loop (RelayDriver.VerifyFix.cs) re-executes with tier escalation on red; FlaggedWorkStore captures the working tree for resume. All this lives in ~15 partial files of RelayDriver across src/VisualRelay.Core/Execution/. The key entry point is RunStage10PreAgentAsync in RelayDriver.Stage9.cs, which orchestrates the three checks and returns a Stage10PreAgentData record with all results.\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Every C# source file must stay under 300 lines (enforced by tools/VisualRelay.Guards) \u2014 new code must be split into focused partial class files.\",\n    \"The nono sandbox (Landlock/Seatbelt) restricts filesystem access at the kernel level; all code must work within the granted allow-list.\",\n    \"GUI observability goes through RelayEvent structured events (Data dictionaries); persistent cross-run state requires file writes per the artifact contract.\",\n    \"Artifact naming convention is load-bearing: verify outputs follow stageN-attemptM.verify-output.txt under .relay/<taskId>/.\",\n    \"The NEEDS-REVIEW marker is the sole queue drain control signal; any new failure surface must not break it.\",\n    \"The 12-stage pipeline in RelayStages.cs is fixed \u2014 a new dedicated 'setup-check' stage cannot be inserted without pipeline redesign.\",\n    \"Bootstrap and guard checks are opt-in via RelayConfig (null \u2192 skip); the system must handle absent checks gracefully.\",\n    \"RelayDriver is split across ~15 partial files; new functionality must follow this partial-class pattern.\",\n    \"Tech stack is C# / .NET 10 / Avalonia; UI changes require Avalonia XAML + view models, backend changes go in VisualRelay.Core.\",\n    \"MaxStageFailures (default 3) caps the fix-verify escalation loop; failure details must fit within this bounded retry budget.\",\n    \"BaselineVerify mode excludes pre-existing failures via git diffing; failure details must distinguish new vs. pre-existing violations.\",\n    \"Test file size guard and BannedApiAnalyzers constraints apply to all new code (no HeadlessUnitTestSession, whole-app tests allowlisted).\"\n  ]\n}\n```",
